# Solana deploy — skills handoff (23 Aug 2026)

You are the **build** agent. A research session installed the deploy skills. Use them; do not invent a stack.

Before any program, wallet, RPC, or deploy work, read:

1. `.agents/skills/solana-dev/SKILL.md` (and the reference it points at for the task). This is the Solana Foundation playbook.
2. `.agents/skills/solana-vulnerability-scanner/SKILL.md` after `anchor test`, before devnet-with-USDC or mainnet.

Also read `AGENTS.md`.

Constraints:

- Venue is **Solana only**. Not Robinhood. Not Base.
- **Never close a program to fund a deploy.** `solana program close` burns the program id permanently and orphans every account it owns. Redeploys upgrade in place onto the same id (`anchor upgrade` / `solana program deploy` with the existing program keypair) — the rent is only tied up, not spent. If the deployer can't cover a deploy, stop and report; do not self-fund from chain state the key controls. Irreversible authority actions (program close, `set-authority`, mint/freeze revocation) need explicit operator approval on every cluster, devnet included.
- Stay on **Anchor 0.32** for the first deploy if the workspace builds. The official skill defaults to 1.1.x — ignore that default until after a working 0.32 deploy. Migration note: `.agents/skills/solana-dev/references/anchor/migrating-v0.32-to-v1.md`.
- Do not install extra Solana skills (Jupiter, Pump, hairyf dumps, GuiBibeau fork).
- Live docs: `https://mcp.solana.com/mcp`.
- First ship: `anchor test` → scanner → `anchor deploy --provider.cluster devnet` → Kit wallet in `apps/web` → keeper resolver key. Mainnet later.
